# Event App API

## Running the application

The application is configured to run using Air for live reloading during development.

### Install Air

```bash
go install github.com/air-verse/air@latest
```

Make sure `$GOPATH/bin` is added to your PATH.

### Air configuration

The project is configured to run from the `cmd/api` directory.

`.air.toml`:

```toml
root = "."
```

### Environment variables

The `.env` file must be located in the same directory where Air is started.

For this project:

```text
cmd/api/.env
```

Example:

```env
PORT=5623
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/event_app?sslmode=disable
JWT_SECRET=your-secret-key
```

### Start application

Navigate to the API directory:

```bash
cd cmd/api
```

Run:

```bash
air
```

The API will be available on:

```text
http://localhost:5623
```

---

## Database migrations

Database schema changes are managed using golang-migrate.

### Install migrate

```bash
go install github.com/golang-migrate/migrate/v4/cmd/migrate@latest
```

### Create a migration

Example:

```bash
migrate create -ext sql -dir ./cmd/migrate/migrations -seq create_attendees_table
```

This command generates two files:

```text
000001_create_attendees_table.up.sql
000001_create_attendees_table.down.sql
```

### Write migration

Example:

`000001_create_attendees_table.up.sql`

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS attendees (
    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    user_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
    event_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
    FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    FOREIGN KEY (event_id) REFERENCES events(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
);
```

`000001_create_attendees_table.down.sql`

```sql
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS attendees;
```

### Apply migrations

```bash
go run main.go up
```

### Rollback migrations

```bash
go run main.go down
```

If a migration fails and the database becomes dirty:

```bash
migrate force <version>
```

Example:

```bash
migrate force 2
```

---

## Swagger Documentation

Swagger documentation is generated using Swaggo.

### Install Swagger CLI

```bash
go install github.com/swaggo/swag/cmd/swag@latest
```

### Generate documentation

Run from the project root:

```bash
swag init --dir cmd/api --parseDependency --parseInternal --parseDepth 1
```

This command generates:

```text
docs/
├── docs.go
├── swagger.json
└── swagger.yaml
```

### Register Swagger

Import the generated package:

```go
import (
    _ "rest_app_in_gin/docs"
)
```

### Swagger endpoint

Documentation is available at:

```text
http://localhost:5623/swagger/index.html
```

### Updating documentation

Whenever API annotations are changed:

```go
// @Summary Get event
// @Description Returns event by ID
// @Router /api/v1/events/{id} [get]
```

regenerate documentation:

```bash
swag init --dir cmd/api --parseDependency --parseInternal --parseDepth 1
```
